# zig-only
# The statusline is clickable end to end: the position chip opens the
# go-to-line prompt, the input-style chip toggles the keymap (the mode
# chip follows), the indent chip prompts for a tab width. At 120x40 the
# statusline is row 38; the right cluster from the edge is utf-8 (7),
# the indent chip (5), the idle bell (3), the input style (10), then
# the position chip (15).
write notes.txt hello world
open notes.txt
expect screen contains "EDIT"
expect screen contains "standard"
expect screen contains "utf-8"
click 85 38
expect screen contains "Go to line"
key esc
click 100 38
expect screen contains "NORMAL"
expect screen contains "vim"
click 100 38
expect screen contains "EDIT"
click 110 38
expect screen contains "Tab width"
key backspace
type "8\n"
expect screen contains "tab width: 8"
